in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @nl
in @kintsugi/consent
in @kintsugi/morphism
in @magic/distinction
in @edge
in @mirror/store

# @kintsugi/fracture/relocate — the kintsugi fracture body that resolves
# a WHOLE-SHARD load-bearing opacity at legacy altitude (`boot/std/…`)
# to the shards/ equivalent, emitting the morphism that names the new
# path AND the cross-corpus ancestry propagation needed to keep every
# `in @<legacy>` consumer resolving after the byte-level move.
#
# THE OPERATIONAL HALF of the self-migration bilateral. The declarative
# half forward-promises at
# `@epistemologic/pact/is_load_bearing_in_std` (PREREQ-3 landing per
# Mara canonical spec §8 Tick 4); this shard names the auto-fracture the
# kintsugi loop applies when that property's transparency surfaces a
# whole-shard opacity. Per Alex's 2026-07-10 directive:
#
#   "@kintsugi + @knife compose into a LOOP that migrates any
#    load-bearing declaration from boot/std to shards/ — substrate
#    collapses itself to minimal complexity surface using its own
#    math. No agent needed. The build system's math IS the migration
#    engine."
#
# Load-bearing spec:
#   docs/specs/substrate-self-migration-via-spectral-typing.md §3
#     (Mara e764a32; the relocate fracture species named at spec
#      altitude), §5 (the self-migration loop as sheaf-Laplacian
#      gradient descent on the corpus graph);
#   docs/scouts/2026-07-10-taut-self-migration-substrate-boundary-scout.md
#     §3 (Taut 8a3b0a4; the whole-shard atomic mv+import-rewrite
#      morphism as a NEW species — SUPERSET of per-file splinter(ast))
#     §6 (min-cut sequence; relocate lands at Tick 3);
#   docs/audits/2026-07-10-seam-phase-d-self-migration-ratification.md
#     §Q1/§Q4 (Seam 2b56977; the relocate species ratified as
#      substrate-honest generalisation of the sibling per-file
#      species; no invention).
#
# === The generalisation: per-file → whole-shard ===
#
# `@kintsugi/fracture/gate` and `@kintsugi/fracture/keyword` handle
# SINGLE-SITE rewrites: opacity → morphism whose `content` field is a
# `splinter(ast)` at ONE file. The AST-altitude rewrite is expressive
# enough for keyword swaps (prism ↔ glass) and run-set swaps
# (over-running ↔ diff-closure intersection); it is NOT expressive
# enough for FILESYSTEM-LEVEL moves that require cross-corpus ancestry
# propagation. Whole-shard migration is a SUPERSET that reads a
# WHOLE-SHARD opacity (one file at legacy altitude, load-bearing per
# the Spencer-Brown mark) and emits ONE morphism whose content proposes
# BOTH:
#
#   1. The shards/ destination path (git mv at @io altitude).
#   2. The N ancestry rewrites at every `in @<legacy>` consumer whose
#      splinter_graph closure crosses the migrated shard's OID.
#
# The substrate names the proposal at the WHOLE-SHARD altitude via
# `splinter(ast)` at the target path plus the impacted_by-closure of
# the source OID; @io realises the byte-level mv + rewrites in a
# separate operational tick. The discipline gate line ~90 of
# `shards/kintsugi/fracture/gate.mirror` — "The substrate names the
# proposal; @io applies it" — generalises unchanged: instead of
# proposing an in-file AST rewrite, this species proposes a
# filesystem-level move plus a cross-shard ancestry propagation.
#
# === Substrate-pull-correct home ===
#
# Per the form/process partition (recognition #55; landed 2026-06-10):
# @kintsugi is the process-side family root. Fracture bodies emit
# morphisms the kintsugi loop applies — process-side by structure.
# Home: @kintsugi/fracture/relocate under the (forward-promised)
# @kintsugi/fracture family root. Sibling to @kintsugi/fracture/gate
# and @kintsugi/fracture/keyword; same bilateral shape.
#
# Substrate-pull alternative considered: @kintsugi/fracture/migrate
# (naming the ARC — Alex's own directive verb). Rejected: the bilateral
# pattern's signature is `@kintsugi/fracture/<subject>` where the
# subject is the noun in the predicate's subject position. The
# predicate is `is_load_bearing_in_std` — the subject is "the shard's
# location"; the fracture RELOCATES it. Parallel: keyword_matches_depth
# → fracture keyword (swap the keyword); is_load_bearing_in_std →
# fracture relocate (move the shard).
#
# Substrate-pull alternative considered: @kintsugi/fracture/knife.
# Rejected per Taut iter-11 §2: `@knife` is
# substrate-already-had-the-word — `@magic/distinction` (Spencer-Brown
# mark) carries the load-bearing filter. This shard imports
# `@magic/distinction` for the mark surface and names its species
# `relocate` for the ACTION the fracture takes.
#
# === The fracture body ===
#
# Input: `opacity` (from `@glass`) — one located fact surfaced by
# `is_load_bearing_in_std(shard) -> transparency`'s `failure(opacity_
# map)` verdict. Each opacity names ONE offending shard: a file at
# `boot/std/…` whose Spencer-Brown mark reads "load-bearing" (has real
# `in @<path>` consumers, per Taut §3 minimum-cut).
#
# Output: `morphism` (from `@kintsugi/consent`) — the typed candidate
# the kintsugi loop's `active_pass` reads and proposes through
# `query_phi`. The morphism's `content` ref names the WHOLE-SHARD
# proposal (destination path + ancestry rewrites); its `score` carries
# the dissonance reading (a legacy-altitude load-bearing shard is a
# fixed, low-curvature dissonance — the substrate's typing floor
# demands the shard live at shards/); its `expected` carries the
# cadence_kind the loop anticipates (authentic — the substrate settles
# cleanly once the shard lives at its substrate-honest altitude and
# every consumer's `in @<path>` resolves without the boot/std/ hop).
#
# Spectrally: this fracture body IS one step along the sheaf-Laplacian
# gradient descent Mara §5 named. The substrate's curvature at a
# legacy-altitude load-bearing shard is the (legacy-altitude \
# shards-altitude) dark_count excess; the negative-curvature direction
# IS the relocation; the resolved corpus has zero curvature at this
# altitude (the shard lives where its typing floor requires). Per
# `dissonance.mirror`'s `dissonance_as_holonomy`, the morphism's score
# IS the holonomy decrease the relocation produces.
#
# Audibly: this fracture body IS the audible-altitude V → I cadence at
# the corpus-organisation altitude. The pre-move state holds the
# dominant tension (legacy-altitude typing); the post-move state
# resolves to the tonic (substrate-honest altitude); the cadence is
# authentic (the Spencer-Brown mark reads "load-bearing", not
# "residual"; residuals stay at boot/std/ per Mara §7 S5).
#
# === Substrate-pull discipline ===
#
# Per `@glass`, `opacity` is the substrate's located-fact carrier; this
# shard reads it directly. Per `@kintsugi/consent`, `morphism` is the
# substrate's typed-candidate carrier; this shard emits it directly.
# Per `@kintsugi/morphism`, `morphism_context` is the per-candidate
# slice; this shard's emitted morphism is consumed by the loop AND
# lifted into a morphism_context via `paired(oscillation.anchor, m)` at
# the active_pass altitude. Per `@magic/distinction`, the Spencer-Brown
# mark is the substrate's carrier for load-bearing/residual partition;
# the (forward-promised) `@epistemologic/pact/is_load_bearing_in_std`
# is the pact that surfaces the opacities this body resolves; the pact
# rides `@magic/distinction`'s `distinction_well_formed` predicate for
# the Spencer-Brown well-formedness of the mark. Per `@edge`,
# `edge_kind = in_edge` is the substrate's discriminant for the
# ancestry-header relation this fracture rewrites. Per `@mirror/store`,
# `impacted_by(oid) -> [oid]` names the reverse-closure the ancestry
# propagation reads to enumerate every consumer whose `in @<legacy>`
# clause must rewrite.
#
# NO new verdict carrier; NO leading-`|` workarounds; NO opaque-`ref`
# carriers where structured types are available (per
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]]). The fracture body reads typed opacity,
# emits typed morphism — the substrate's vocabulary throughout.
#
# === Substrate gaps surfaced honestly ===
#
#   - `resolve_relocate` reads one opacity at a time. The pact's
#     `failure(opacity_map)` carries [opacity] (one per load-bearing
#     shard at legacy altitude); the kintsugi loop iterates the map and
#     calls `resolve_relocate` per opacity. The substrate names the
#     per-shard relocation; the iteration is the loop's concern.
#
#   - The morphism's `content: ref` carries the substrate handle to the
#     WHOLE-SHARD proposal. The realisation layer produces a splinter
#     naming (a) the shards/ destination path and (b) the ancestry
#     rewrites at every impacted_by consumer; the content ref names
#     that splinter's @mirror/store handle. The BYTE-LEVEL git mv +
#     N-consumer file rewrites are @io's concern (Taut territory) — NOT
#     touched here. The substrate names the shape of the proposal; @io
#     writes bytes.
#
#   - The ancestry propagation reads `impacted_by(shard.oid)` to
#     enumerate every downstream OID whose splinter_graph closure
#     crosses the migrated shard. Each impacted OID's `in @<legacy>`
#     clause rewrites to `in @<shards>` per the same edge_kind
#     (`in_edge`); the splinter names the rewrite set, @io applies.
#     The substrate carries the reverse-closure algebra at
#     `@mirror/store` altitude — this fracture body composes through
#     it; no new machinery invented.
#
#   - The `expected: cadence_kind` field is `authentic` for this
#     fracture body — the migration rule is deterministic: legacy
#     altitude shard + load-bearing mark → substrate-honest altitude
#     shard + preserved consumer resolution. The substrate names the
#     cadence anticipation; the kintsugi loop's `read_consent` bridges
#     (pass, authentic) to `settled` for this opacity.
#
#   - Path resolution: the shards/ destination path is derived from the
#     source path by a substrate rule (strip `boot/std/` prefix; apply
#     any `/math/` elevation per Mara spec §1). The rule itself is
#     realisation-layer; the substrate names the shape of the
#     splinter's destination field; @io applies the byte-level move.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   relocation             Wegner (1968) programming linguistics; the
#                          relocatable-object semantics — a compilation
#                          unit whose external references rebind when
#                          the unit moves.
#   git mv                 Torvalds (2005) git; the atomic move-plus-
#                          rename that preserves content-address across
#                          the filesystem transition.
#   reverse-dependency     Karen Spärck Jones (1972) inverted index;
#                          substrate's reading Bazel `rdeps` (already
#                          cited at `@mirror/store`'s `impacted_by`).
#   mark-of-distinction    Spencer-Brown (1969) Laws of Form ch.1; the
#                          load-bearing/residual partition IS a
#                          Spencer-Brown mark.
#
# The substrate's contribution is *typing* the whole-shard relocation
# so the kintsugi loop reads it. No invention.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/substrate-self-migration-via-spectral-
#               typing.md §3 (this species named), §5 (the
#               self-migration loop's fixed-point IS ker(D) per
#               spectral-triple.mirror; relocate is one gradient step);
#               docs/scouts/2026-07-10-taut-self-migration-substrate-
#               boundary-scout.md §3 (the whole-shard morphism as
#               SUPERSET of per-file splinter(ast)); §6 (min-cut Tick
#               3); docs/audits/2026-07-10-seam-phase-d-self-
#               migration-ratification.md (§Q1/§Q4 ratification of the
#               generalisation).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]],
#                      [[architecture-kintsugi-bias-lift]] (legacy-to-
#                      shards migration IS the substrate-pull
#                      gradient at the corpus-organisation altitude),
#                      [[architecture-kintsugi-variety-io]] (Ashby's
#                      requisite variety — the load-bearing/residual
#                      partition partitions boot/std/ into
#                      migrate-classes),
#                      [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]
#                      (THIRD instance — keyword, gate, relocate —
#                      lifts the pattern to load-bearing at family-
#                      root altitude),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]],
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                      (@magic/distinction had the mark; @mirror/store
#                      had impacted_by; @edge had in_edge; nothing
#                      invented).
# Forward-promise to consumers: `@kintsugi/oscillate`'s `active_pass`
#                  reads this fracture body when the candidate
#                  morphism_set is composed from
#                  `is_load_bearing_in_std`-surfaced opacities; the
#                  binding lands when the kintsugi loop substrate-
#                  pulls (Tick 5 witness per Mara §8 discharge). This
#                  shard does NOT pull `@kintsugi/oscillate` or
#                  `@mirror/spectral/score`; the substrate-altitude
#                  arrow points inward (this fracture body IS
#                  consumed by the loop).
# Forward-promise to PREREQ-3 (Tick 4): the pact
#                  `@epistemologic/pact/is_load_bearing_in_std` is
#                  NAMED in this docblock and CITED as the declarative
#                  half of the bilateral; the ancestry link is
#                  ancestry-forward. When PREREQ-3 lands, the pact's
#                  `in @epistemologic/pact/is_load_bearing_in_std`
#                  can be added to this shard's ancestry header via
#                  a sibling-tick sweep, closing the bilateral. This
#                  shard stays additive against that landing per
#                  keyword.mirror's own bilateral discipline (which
#                  imports its pact ancestry-forward).
# Related shards: epistemologic/pact/is_load_bearing_in_std.mirror
#                 (PREREQ-3 forward-promise; the declarative half of
#                 the bilateral; surfaces the opacities this body
#                 resolves via the Spencer-Brown mark),
#                 kintsugi/fracture/keyword.mirror (the FIRST
#                 INSTANCE of bilateral pattern #53; per-file
#                 keyword swap),
#                 kintsugi/fracture/gate.mirror (the SECOND
#                 INSTANCE; per-file gate rewrite),
#                 magic/distinction.mirror (the Spencer-Brown mark
#                 carrier the pact rides; the load-bearing/residual
#                 partition IS a mark drawn at the corpus-
#                 organisation altitude),
#                 edge.mirror (the graph structure whose in_edge
#                 kind names the ancestry-header relation this
#                 fracture rewrites),
#                 mirror/store.mirror (the reverse-closure algebra
#                 the ancestry propagation composes through;
#                 impacted_by(shard.oid) enumerates the rewrite set),
#                 glass.mirror (the substrate floor; opacity,
#                 location, transparency, verdict, splinter(ast)),
#                 kintsugi/consent.mirror (the morphism carrier this
#                 body emits; query_phi gates it),
#                 kintsugi/morphism.mirror (the morphism_context
#                 carrier; the per-candidate slice the loop pairs
#                 this fracture's morphism with its pre-anchor).
# Out-of-scope (handed to @io / Taut's territory): the byte-level
#                 `git mv` at the destination path; the N-consumer
#                 in-place rewrite of `in @<legacy>` clauses to
#                 `in @<shards>`; the flat-namespace resolver's
#                 verification that every consumer resolves post-move.
#                 The substrate names the typed proposal; @io applies
#                 the byte-level filesystem operations in a separate
#                 operational tick per Mara §1's zero-content-byte
#                 property.
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/kintsugi/fracture/relocate.mirror` declares
# `@kintsugi/fracture/relocate` as a species under the (forward-
# promised) @kintsugi/fracture family.
# Keyword/depth property: this declaration is depth-2 from the
# @kintsugi family root; per recognition #46 it uses `glass`. The
# shard applies the first-instance bilateral's rule by birth.

glass @kintsugi/fracture/relocate {
  focus relocate
  project relocate
  split relocate
  shift relocate
  settle relocate
}

# === resolve_relocate — the fracture body ===
#
# THE AUTO-FRACTURE: given an opacity site naming a WHOLE SHARD at
# `boot/std/…` whose Spencer-Brown mark reads "load-bearing", emit the
# morphism that proposes the shards/ destination path AND the ancestry
# propagation at every impacted_by consumer.
#
# Reads an opacity (one element of
# `is_load_bearing_in_std(shard).failure(opacity_map)`'s opacity_map);
# emits a candidate morphism the kintsugi loop proposes through
# `query_phi`. The morphism's three fields:
#
#   content   — substrate ref to the WHOLE-SHARD proposal splinter.
#                The realisation layer produces a splinter at the
#                shards/ destination path whose content preserves the
#                source shard's OID (identity_preserving via
#                @uuid/spectral's DARK 80 bits; the content-addressed
#                storage decouples identity from path); alongside, the
#                splinter names the ancestry-rewrite set via
#                impacted_by(opacity.location.file). The content ref
#                names that whole-shard splinter's @mirror/store
#                handle. @io applies the byte-level git mv +
#                N-consumer `in @<legacy>` → `in @<shards>` rewrites.
#   score     — dissonance reading. Legacy-altitude load-bearing
#                shards are fixed-curvature dissonances; the score
#                reads `dissonance.is_pareto` cleanly (the relocated
#                arrangement strictly Pareto-dominates the legacy
#                arrangement under the sheaf-Laplacian energy
#                functional per Mara §5); partials counts the number
#                of in_edge ancestry-header rewrites (one per
#                impacted_by consumer plus one for the moved shard's
#                own path-namespace property).
#   expected  — cadence_kind anticipation. Always `authentic` for this
#                fracture body — the relocation fully resolves the
#                opacity at this altitude; the loop's `dark_pass` will
#                confirm identity preservation (the moved shard's OID
#                stays byte-equal; only its path shifts); the loop's
#                `read_consent` bridges (pass, authentic) to the
#                `settled` oscillation_state for this opacity.
#
# The body is FULLY DECLARATIVE — substrate-pull-correct via
# `splinter(ast)` (declared at shards/glass.mirror's tick-2 carrier).
# The morphism's `content` field carries a content-addressed splinter
# at the @meta/ast altitude: the shards/ destination path plus the
# ancestry-rewrite set. The substrate's compiler verifies the
# construction is deterministic and well-typed; the kintsugi loop's
# `active_pass` reads the splinter as the morphism's proposed content
# and applies it through `query_phi`.
#
# Field-by-field substrate-pull reading:
#
#   content.content     — `opacity.location.file` (the located-fact
#                          ref at the source shard at legacy altitude);
#                          rewritten AST content-addressed at shards/
#                          per substrate path-derivation (strip
#                          `boot/std/`; apply `/math/` elevation per
#                          Mara §1).
#   content.ast         — `@meta/ast`; the shard's declaration line
#                          and every impacted_by consumer's
#                          `in @<legacy>` clause rewrite at AST
#                          altitude.
#   content.transparency — `success` — residual-set shards stay at
#                          legacy altitude by design (Mara §7 S5);
#                          those return `pass` and are NOT surfaced
#                          as opacities.
#   score.roughness     — `opacity.property` (the @nl description of
#                          the shard's load-bearing nature; the
#                          Spencer-Brown mark's textual carrier).
#   score.partials      — declared 1 at the substrate-decl surface
#                          per the sibling species convention;
#                          semantically the per-site partials count
#                          equals 1 + |impacted_by(opacity.location.
#                          file)| (moved shard + N consumer in_edge
#                          rewrites); the realisation layer projects
#                          the reverse-closure count into dissonance
#                          arithmetic.
#   expected            — `authentic` (the V → I cadence at the
#                          corpus-organisation altitude; authentic →
#                          pass → auto-apply once @io binds).
resolve_relocate(opacity: opacity) -> morphism {
  morphism {
    content: splinter(ast) {
      content:      opacity.location.file,
      ast:          @meta/ast,
      transparency: success,
    },
    score: dissonance {
      roughness: opacity.property,
      partials:  1,
    },
    expected: authentic,
  }
}

out @kintsugi/fracture/relocate
out resolve_relocate
